node_modules/

# The calculator's source USED TO BE ignored here, and the reason was sound
# while it lasted: the build encrypted the app, tools/ is served by GitHub
# Pages, and committing the plaintext would have published the very thing
# calculator/index.html was there to encrypt.
#
# The build moved to database mode and the reason went with it. The published
# calculator/index.html and tools/calc/app.html are the same bytes apart from
# a base path and a publishable key, which is public by design — so the rule
# was hiding a file that was already published, and its only remaining effect
# was that ten thousand lines had no revision history and lived on one disk.
#
# So it is tracked. The source carries __SUPABASE_URL__ and
# __SUPABASE_ANON_KEY__ as placeholders and no secret of any kind — checked,
# not assumed — so it publishes strictly less than the built page does.
#
# If the build ever goes back to encrypting (no database, per-user
# passphrases), this rule has to come back with it.

# Python bytecode. These were committed by accident back in the trilingual
# work and rebuilt on every run, so every build showed a spurious diff.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
